BY DESIGN, NOT BY MERIT. This directory is the CONTROL arm of
test-defcon2-holdfire-garrison. Its rules.yaml differs from the treatment's by exactly one
quantity -- DefconEscalation.ModeDefault, Escalation -> Skirmish -- and
DefconEscalationState's constructor answers that with `Level = NoLevel` (0), so
DefconFireDiscipline.HoldsFire(0) is false and GarrisonManager.ScanForTarget (read site 5)
runs normally.

An empty port deploys as soon as that scanner returns a target which survives
TargetConfirmTicks (10) across TargetScanInterval (8) -- ~30 ticks from the house flipping to
Russia. The hold window is 300 ticks, ten times that, so this arm fails on a manned port long
before it could fail for want of time. FAIL is the only outcome it can honestly produce.

WHY IT EXISTS. A green treatment is not evidence unless something could have made it red
(AUTOTEST.md). Without this arm, "the garrison did nothing" is indistinguishable from "nothing
was ever going to happen here" -- and for a garrison that is not a hypothetical worry: the
sibling scenario test-human-autoacquires-garrisoned-house keeps its garrison in shelter by
THREE independent mechanisms that have nothing to do with DEFCON (the building's own AutoTarget
held at HoldFire, and a probe placed sixteen cells out, beyond the shelter soldiers' 10c0).
Any one of them arriving here by a careless edit would make the treatment pass for the wrong
reason, and this arm is what would notice.

A PASS HERE IS LOUDLY RED AND FALSIFIES THE TREATMENT, NOT THIS FILE. The two setup facts to
check first, in this order, because they are the ones a copy-edit breaks:
  1. V01 must have NO AutoTarget in either rules.yaml. ^CivBuilding ships none, which is what
     leaves the building on FireAtWill via `autoTarget?.Stance ?? UnitStance.FireAtWill`.
  2. The humvee must be INSIDE the shelter soldiers' 10c0 envelope (it is placed ~6.5 cells
     out). Past ten cells, ScanForTarget finds nothing and no port deploys in either arm.
Report and stop on a pass; do not widen the window or re-run hoping for the other answer.

THE ONE FAILURE THIS DECLARATION MUST NOT ABSORB, because it produces the declared outcome
for the wrong reason: a staging fault. Verdicts beginning `fail: SETUP` (house not Neutral,
probe out of envelope, no EnterTransport order offered, house and humvee not a live targeting
pair, match opened at DEFCON 3 or 1) and `fail: STAGING` (the riflemen never reached the
shelter) are faults in BOTH directories, not this arm doing its job. Read the reason string.

The verdict line to expect carries `defcon=0` in its census and `ports` above zero. If it
reads `defcon=2` the override did not merge and this directory is a second copy of the
treatment.

REMOVE THIS FILE only if the control legitimately starts passing, which would mean the map can
no longer separate the two hypotheses and needs new geometry rather than a new declaration. A
hang, a crash, or a run that never reaches a verdict still reds under it.
